							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371567+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371567+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "6kVbHbwMQTCyc7Z0YtxF4A=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "Some problems in a GT image only show while they happen: a slow UI, a process that hangs, many garbage collections, memory that grows. A report captures such a moment as plain data, so that it can be looked at later, possibly in another image than the one where it happened."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371595+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371595+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "tt1xZ2tlSNCtM1sOmPr5ww=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "The infrastructure keeps four things apart, because they change for different reasons: **what** is recorded (the report), **how and when** it is recorded (the recorder), **where** it is kept (the store), and **how it is found and read again** (the metadata). Recording reports is on {{gtPage:GT reports available for data collection}}, analysing them on {{gtPage:Analysing stored GT reports}}. The classes are in {{gtPackage:GToolkit-Utility-SpaceTally}}, {{gtPackage:GToolkit-Utility-GarbageCollectAnalysis}} and {{gtPackage:GToolkit-Utility-Basic}}."
						}
					]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371474+01:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371474+01:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "Yf6ie/EHSFirUPkczPnqpg=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Why reports"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371601+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371601+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "C6aYfC4sSgWc1GTV3YNZUg=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "| Piece | Classes | Responsibility | Why it is separate |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Report | {{gtClass:GtProcessesReport}}, {{gtClass:GtMessageTallyReport}}, {{gtClass:GtGarbageCollectsReport}}, {{gtClass:GtSpaceTallyReport}} | the recorded data, its image data and its report uid; writes its own files ({{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#writeFilesTo:|label=#selector}}) and reads itself back ({{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport class>>#fromStoredFiles:|label=#selector}}) | a report is a plain object: create it, inspect it, and only then decide whether to store it |\n| Image data | {{gtClass:GtReportImageData}} | the GT, GT VM, Pharo VM and Pharo image versions | every report says which image it came from, without identifying the user or the machine |\n| Recorder | {{gtClass:GtReportRecorder}} and its subclasses | how one kind of report is recorded: {{gtMethod:GtReportRecorder>>#recordReport|label=#selector}} (the time-sensitive part) and {{gtMethod:GtReportRecorder>>#completeReport:|label=#selector}} (the slow part) | the same report can be recorded with other settings or other image data |\n| Recording | {{gtClass:GtReportRecording}} | one background run of a recorder into a store; announces its start and end ({{gtClass:GtReportRecordingStarted}}, {{gtClass:GtReportRecordingEnded}}); holds the report and the entry, or the error | recording must not block the UI, and a Message Tally must see what the UI does |\n| Store | {{gtClass:GtReportsStore}}: {{gtClass:GtReportsLocalStore}}, {{gtClass:GtReportsCompositeStore}}, {{gtClass:GtNoReportsStore}} | where reports go: the folder layout, the storage id, writing text and bytes ({{gtMethod:GtReportsLocalStore>>#write:to:|label=#selector}}, {{gtMethod:GtReportsLocalStore>>#writeBytes:to:|label=#selector}}) | a report does not know where it is kept |\n| Entry | {{gtClass:GtReportsStoreEntry}} with {{gtClass:GtReportsStoreDataFile}} and {{gtClass:GtReportsStoreMetadataFile}} | one stored copy: its folder, the files written (size and write time) and the metadata | shows what was written, without keeping the contents in memory |\n| Metadata | {{gtClass:GtReportMetadata}}, {{gtClass:GtReportFileDescription}} | `meta.json`: report type, class and alias, report uid, storage id, machine name, image data, files with their sizes, format version | reports can be found, grouped and sized without reading their data |\n| Reading back | {{gtClass:GtStoredReportFiles}} and the report's class-side {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport class>>#fromStoredFiles:|label=#selector}} | turns a stored folder back into the report object | an analysis works on the same objects that were recorded |"
						}
					]
				},
