				},
				"string" : "## The pieces"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371605+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371605+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "rNx/STICTJm/7e5L5Lqi7w=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**Recording.** {{gtMethod:GtReportRecorder>>#recordInBackgroundInto:|label=#selector}} on a recorder starts a recording ({{gtMethod:GtReportRecording>>#start|label=#selector}}). The recording runs {{gtMethod:GtReportRecorder>>#recordReport|label=#selector}} at the recording priority, above the UI ({{gtMethod:GtReportRecorder>>#recordingPriority|label=#selector}}); then it lowers its own priority to background and runs {{gtMethod:GtReportRecorder>>#completeReport:|label=#selector}} and {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#storeIn:|label=#selector}} ({{gtMethod:GtReportRecording>>#record|label=#selector}}). {{gtMethod:GtReportRecorder>>#createReport|label=#selector}} does the same synchronously, without storing."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371608+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371608+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "wQ/fE60LS9WzbgVh6icfcQ=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**Storing.** {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#storeIn:|label=#selector}} on a report asks the store to store it ({{gtMethod:GtReportsStore>>#store:|label=#selector}}): the store creates an entry with a new storage id ({{gtMethod:GtReportsStore>>#entryFor:storageId:|label=#selector}}), the report writes its files into the entry ({{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#writeFilesTo:|label=#selector}}), and the entry writes `meta.json` last ({{gtMethod:GtReportsStoreEntry>>#writeMetadataOf:|label=#selector}}). Every write goes through the entry, which records the file with the number of bytes the store read back from the written file ({{gtMethod:GtReportsStoreEntry>>#record:writing:|label=#selector}}). A composite store creates one entry per store with the same storage id ({{gtMethod:GtReportsCompositeStore>>#entryFor:storageId:|label=#selector}}), so every store gets the same folder name."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.37161+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.37161+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "qkT6E4ACRi2Ra0cKbT7F2A=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**Reading back.** {{gtClass:GtStoredReportFiles}} {{gtMethod:GtStoredReportFiles class>>#folder:|label=#selector}} reads `meta.json`; {{gtMethod:GtStoredReportFiles>>#report|label=#selector}} takes the report class from the metadata ({{gtMethod:GtStoredReportFiles>>#reportClass|label=#selector}}) and asks it for {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport class>>#fromStoredFiles:|label=#selector}}. The folder layout and the content of `meta.json` are described under *Where reports are stored* on {{gtPage:GT reports available for data collection}}."
						}
					]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371603+01:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371603+01:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "NISnCmq6QLyS5lRaGq4hoA=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## From recording to stored files, and back"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371614+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371614+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "w6HISFi8TXisWcW3CwP/Hg=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "- **No common report superclass.** Reports have little in common beyond a small protocol: {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#reportType|label=#selector}}, {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#imageData|label=#selector}}, {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#reportUid|label=#selector}}, {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#writeFilesTo:|label=#selector}}, {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#storeIn:|label=#selector}} and the class-side {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport class>>#fromStoredFiles:|label=#selector}}. Each report implements it, so a new report does not have to fit a hierarchy.\n- **Recording in two steps.** {{gtMethod:GtReportRecorder>>#recordReport|label=#selector}} must be quick and runs high, so that a busy UI does not delay it; completing and storing are slow and run at background priority, so that the UI stays usable meanwhile ({{gtMethod:GtReportRecording>>#record|label=#selector}}). Only one Message Tally can run at a time.\n- **`meta.json` is written last** ({{gtMethod:GtReportsStore>>#store:|label=#selector}}). A folder without it is an interrupted write, never a report.\n- **Report type first in the layout** ({{gtMethod:GtReportsStore>>#folderFor:storageId:machineName:|label=#selector}}). Most questions start from a kind of report. A store that keeps the reports of several machines can add a machine level to the layout; it gets the machine name for every report ({{gtMethod:GtReportsStore>>#machineNameFor:|label=#selector}}). Ids and date folders are in UTC, so that images in different time zones sort together.\n- **No identifying data in GT.** {{gtClass:GtReportImageData}} holds only versions and an empty machine name ({{gtMethod:GtReportImageData>>#machineName|label=#selector}}); a subclass can add more where that is wanted, and a recorder decides which image data its reports get ({{gtMethod:GtReportRecorder class>>#imageData:|label=#selector}}).\n- **Two ids.** The storage id names one stored copy ({{gtMethod:GtReportsStore>>#newStorageId|label=#selector}}). The report uid is a {{gtClass:UUID}} given in the report's {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#initialize|label=#selector}} and kept by every copy, so copies can be recognised and analysed once.\n- **Class name plus alias.** The metadata names the report class ({{gtMethod:GtReportMetadata>>#reportClassName|label=#selector}}), to read the report back, and its {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport class>>#leJsonV4Name|label=#selector}} as a stable alias ({{gtMethod:GtReportMetadata>>#reportAlias|label=#selector}}), to read it back after the class is renamed.\n- **Nothing large in memory.** Entries keep where and how much was written, not what ({{gtClass:GtReportsStoreFile}}); the sizes come from the written files.\n- **The format version is a label.** Every `meta.json` carries {{gtMethod:GtReportMetadata>>#formatVersion|label=#selector}} ({{gtMethod:GtReportMetadata class>>#currentFormatVersion|label=#selector}}); no code branches on it yet. When the format changes, read the version from the plain JSON first and pick a reader for it, because {{gtClass:LeJsonV4}} reads the file into the current class before the version is known."
						}
					]
				},
