				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Design decisions and their intent"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371619+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:28:28.371619+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "SARPYNkoQWWthuEUoyMjEw=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "1. **Write the report class**, without a superclass, following {{gtClass:GtProcessesReport}}:\n   - slots for the data, plus `imageData` and `reportUid`; in {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#initialize|label=#selector}} set `imageData := GtReportImageData new` ({{gtClass:GtReportImageData}}) and `reportUid := UUID new`;\n   - {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#reportType|label=#selector}} answers the folder name, lowercase with dashes;\n   - {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#writeFilesTo:|label=#selector}} writes the files: {{gtMethod:GtReportsStoreEntry>>#writeJsonOf:|label=#selector}} for most reports, {{gtMethod:GtReportsStoreEntry>>#writeText:extension:|label=#selector}} for text, {{gtMethod:GtReportsStoreEntry>>#writeGzippedStonOf:|label=#selector}} for large object graphs, {{gtMethod:GtReportsStoreEntry>>#writeBytes:named:extension:|label=#selector}} for several files of one kind;\n   - the class-side {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport class>>#fromStoredFiles:|label=#selector}} reads them back ({{gtMethod:GtStoredReportFiles>>#readJson|label=#selector}}, {{gtMethod:GtStoredReportFiles>>#readText:|label=#selector}}, {{gtMethod:GtStoredReportFiles>>#readGzippedSton|label=#selector}}, {{gtMethod:GtStoredReportFiles>>#readBytesNamed:extension:|label=#selector}});\n   - the class-side {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport class>>#leJsonV4Name|label=#selector}} gives a stable name; run {{gtClass:LeJsonV4}} {{gtMethod:LeJsonV4 class>>#cleanUniqueInstance|label=#selector}} after adding it or after changing slots. The JSON reader sets every written slot through a setter of the same name, so each one needs a setter (e.g. {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#reportUid:|label=#selector}}); a class-side `leJsonV4AttributeMapping` leaves out slots that must not be written (like the live tally of {{gtMethod:GtMessageTallyReport class>>#leJsonV4AttributeMapping}});\n   - {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#storeIn:|label=#selector}} answers `aStore store: self`; add {{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#printOn:|label=#selector}} and a summary view, so that the report is useful in the inspector before it is stored.\n2. **Write a recorder** only when recording needs settings or must run in the background: subclass {{gtClass:GtReportRecorder}} and implement {{gtMethod:GtReportRecorder>>#recordReport|label=#selector}}, plus {{gtMethod:GtReportRecorder>>#completeReport:|label=#selector}} for slow work (e.g. {{gtClass:GtMessageTallyReportRecorder}}).\n3. **Check it** with examples that store the report in a memory store ({{gtClass:GtReportsLocalStore}} {{gtMethod:GtReportsLocalStore class>>#rootFolder:|label=#selector}} with `FileSystem memory root / 'gt-reports'`) and read it back (see {{gtClass:GtReportsStoreExamples}} and {{gtClass:GtStoredReportFilesExamples}}).\n4. **Document it**: add a section to {{gtPage:GT reports available for data collection}}, with one sentence on what the report shows, a snippet that creates it and one that stores it."
						},
						{
