							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "A store decides where reports go, for example a remote file service. Subclass {{gtClass:GtReportsStore}} and implement:\n\n- {{gtMethod:GtReportsStore>>#rootFolder|label=#selector}}: the root of the layout, any object that answers `/` like a file reference;\n- {{gtMethod:GtReportsStore>>#write:to:|label=#selector}} and {{gtMethod:GtReportsStore>>#writeBytes:to:|label=#selector}}: write the text or bytes and answer the number of bytes written, read back from the written file (as {{gtMethod:GtReportsLocalStore>>#write:to:|label=#selector}} does), because that number goes into the metadata;\n- {{gtMethod:GtReportsStore>>#description|label=#selector}}: a short name shown in the entries and recordings;\n- optionally {{gtMethod:GtReportsStore>>#machineName|label=#selector}} and {{gtMethod:GtReportsStore>>#folderFor:storageId:machineName:|label=#selector}}, to add a machine level to the layout.\n\nThe entries, file objects, metadata and composite stores then work without changes."
